=== email subject
[Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] 1 actively exploited flaw in your products and 1 end-of-life release
=== email body
Patchtacio found 1 known exploited vulnerability (CISA KEV) that affects products on your list. Attackers are already using it. Start with the earliest deadline.
Patchtacio matched it by product name and has not checked whether your versions are affected.
It also found 1 release you run at or near the end of security support (endoflife.date).

New:
1. [Action needed by 12 Oct 2026] Fortinet FortiOS: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2026-24858)
   Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel Vulnerability. Added to CISA's list 28 Sep 2026.
   What to do: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
   If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, follow applicable BOD 22-01 guidance for cloud services, or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
   Details: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24858

End of life:
1. [End of life since 30 Sep 2026] Microsoft Windows Server 2016: security updates have stopped
   Security updates for Microsoft Windows Server 2016 stopped on 30 Sep 2026: newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, are not fixed any more. Extended support (often paid) is listed until 30 Sep 2029.
   What to do: Upgrade to a supported release. The vendor's lifecycle page says which releases are supported; see https://endoflife.date/windows-server
   Acknowledge with: patchtacio ack eol/microsoft-windows-server/2016

For each entry, CISA's deadline is the one it set for US government agencies. Use it as a guide to how urgent each one is.

--
When you have dealt with one, run: patchtacio ack <CVE ID or ID shown>, for example: patchtacio ack CVE-2026-24858
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Fortinet FortiOS (FortiGate firewalls) and Microsoft Windows Server are on your Patchtacio product list.
